    "body": "## Problem\n\nOpening a file whose line ends with an invalid multibyte lead byte aborts an ASan build during startup with a heap-buffer-overflow read (#42559). Minimal reproducer: a file containing exactly the bytes `D8 83 FD` (`printf '\\330\\203\\375' > input.dat`), opened with `nvim -b -n --clean input.dat`.\n\nTrace: `utf_ClusterInfo_impl` (mbyte.c) ← `utf_ClusterInfo` (mbyte.h) ← `linesize_fast` (plines.c) during `comp_botline`.\n\nRoot cause, confirmed by instrumenting the walk:\n\n1. The line is `D8 83` (U+0603, grapheme class Prepend) followed by `0xFD`, whose `utf8len_tab` entry announces a 6-byte sequence. The line buffer is 3 bytes + NUL.\n2. `utf_ptr2CharInfo_impl` correctly rejects `0xFD` (the next byte is NUL, not a continuation) and returns -1.\n3. `utf_iscomposing(0x0603, -1)` still reports \"composing\": `utf8proc_grapheme_break_stateful` feeds -1 to `utf8proc_get_property`, which yields a default property, and the break state machine reports \"no break\" against a Prepend base.\n4. `utf_ClusterInfo_impl` therefore advances `next` by the *declared* length (6 bytes) instead of stopping, and its post-advance `*next` check reads past the end of the line buffer. With `max_len` = INT_MAX (how NUL-terminated callers like `linesize_fast` invoke it), the declared length is the only thing that could have stopped the walk.\n\n## Solution\n\nTreat an undecodable byte as a cluster break: it is not a code point and cannot compose with the base character. One condition added at the call site in `utf_ClusterInfo_impl`:\n\n```c\nif (next_code < 0 || !utf_iscomposing(prev_code, next_code, &state)) {\n```\n\nThis stops the walk at the invalid byte and the existing `-1`-aware return (`.len = 1`) takes care of the rest.\n\n## Test\n\nRegression test added to `test/functional/ui/multibyte_spec.lua`: writes a file containing `\\216\\131\\253` (`D8 83 FD`), opens it, and asserts the screen renders (`؃?`). Before the fix this crashes an ASan-instrumented binary during startup.\n\nVerified locally on macOS arm64 (commit 54f94d6fc, ASan+UBSan build):\n\n- The reproducer aborts on master (`heap-buffer-overflow ... READ of size 1 ... utf_ClusterInfo_impl mbyte.c:1843`) and with this patch the same file opens and renders normally, no ASan output.\n- `make functionaltest-lua TEST_FILE=test/functional/ui/multibyte_spec.lua`: 22/22 pass, including the new test.\n- `clang-format --dry-run src/nvim/mbyte.c` is clean.\n\nFixes #42559\n",
    "closed_at": "2026-10-27T19:18:00Z",
