            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "no comment is needed when there is no mystery around the condition. \n\ncallers of `utf_ptr2CharInfo_impl` must _always_ check the return value as called out in its own doc comment (it is like an implicit error union), there is _nothing_ special for this caller except than I forgor to check this edge case:p",
            "commit_id": "153eac32dd194ed07be99c3894d57eee712e7ce9",
            "copilot_code_review_sources": [],
            "created_at": "2026-10-27T18:51:37Z",
            "diff_hunk": "@@ -1805,7 +1805,12 @@ ClusterInfo utf_ClusterInfo_impl(StrCharInfo base, int *max_len)\n     }\n \n     int32_t const next_code = utf_ptr2CharInfo_impl(next, (uintptr_t)next_len);\n-    if (!utf_iscomposing(prev_code, next_code, &state)) {\n+    // An undecodable byte is not a code point and cannot join the cluster.\n+    // Composing state machines only know real code points; feeding them -1\n+    // can report \"no break\", which would advance next by the DECLARED\n+    // sequence length (utf8len_tab) even when fewer bytes remain, running\n+    // past the end of the NUL-terminated line buffer.",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/neovim/neovim/pull/42560#discussion_r4392829859",
